::ENG2_U04_L08_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.RS.01] Source set: Source A says a pilot report found fewer unwanted trays after staff used student selections. Source B says reminders helped more students complete the form. Which synthesis is strongest?{
=A. The sources show that pre-order forms can reduce unwanted trays when students complete the forms consistently.#Correct. This combines the outcome from Source A with the support from Source B.
~B. The sources are about lunch and forms.#Incorrect. This is too general.
~C. The sources prove all waste will end forever.#Incorrect. This overstates the evidence.
~D. The sources do not connect.#Incorrect. The sources both support the same research workflow.
}

::ENG2_U04_L08_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.W.03] Which sentence best explains why the pilot report matters?{
~A. The report has words about trays.#Incorrect. This is vague.
=B. The report matters because it connects student selections to fewer unwanted trays.#Correct. This explains how the evidence answers the research question.
~C. Reports are always correct.#Incorrect. This is an unsupported absolute statement.
~D. Lunch exists at school.#Incorrect. This does not explain evidence.
}

::ENG2_U04_L08_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.W.04] Which revision is best for a student-facing publication?{
~A. Pre-order compliance optimizes cafeteria outcomes.#Incorrect. This is too formal.
~B. The form thing helps stuff.#Incorrect. This is too vague.
=C. Completing the form helps staff prepare meals students are more likely to choose.#Correct. This keeps the meaning clear for students.
~D. Food-service systems require procedural alignment.#Incorrect. This is unclear for the intended audience.
}

::ENG2_U04_L08_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.C.03] Which publication plan best fits the Unit 4 workflow?{
~A. Copy an entire report and add a random picture.#Incorrect. This does not synthesize or adapt for audience.
~B. Use a decorative poster with no source evidence.#Incorrect. The product must be source-based.
~C. Write only private notes and do not publish.#Incorrect. The workflow includes publication.
=D. Use reliable evidence, explain it in student-friendly language, and add a labeled chart that supports the finding.#Correct. This connects research, writing, revision, and publication.
}

::ENG2_U04_L08_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.L.01] Which sentence is complete and polished?{
~A. Because the chart shows fewer trays.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
=B. The chart shows fewer unwanted trays after the pre-order pilot, which supports the source-based message.#Correct. This sentence is complete and clear.
~C. Chart trays pilot because.#Incorrect. This is unclear.
~D. The report, the chart, and students.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
}
